    {
        "text": "A non fungible token, or nft, is a type of cryptographic token representing a unique asset. NFTs are tokenized certificates of digital or real world assets. They function as verifiable proofs of authenticity and ownership using a blockchain network. NFTs are non fungible, which means they are not interchangeable with each other. Such a feature introduces scarcity to the digital world. On the other hand, all fiat currencies and most cryptocurrencies like Bitcoin and ether are fungible. Being fungible means an asset's individual units are interchangeable and indistinguishable from each other, making them perfect as a medium of exchange.",
        "start": 3760,
        "end": 45740,
        "confidence": 0.9840448,
